WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.940
Welcome to Table Talk, where each week I unpack insights from Christian theology and spirituality

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:11.360
that help you become a thoughtful, contemplative, and downright great human being.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.559
So today I want to talk to you about five reasons why people don't read the Bible and

00:00:16.559 --> 00:00:18.440
how to fix that.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:25.360
So the first is that at some point in the past, they tried and became discouraged.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:31.040
They heard that anyone could open up the Word of God and understand everything on the first

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.040
reading.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:37.639
And they jumped in, and somewhere in the midst of Leviticus, they got totally lost.

00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:40.080
The Bible is not an easy book.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.860
However, that leads us to the second reason people don't read the Bible.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.720
They heard it was impossibly difficult.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:50.400
They heard that you need a PhD in ancient literature to understand it.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.080
Again, I think that's a misconception.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:59.360
The truth is somewhere in the middle between it's super easy or it's impossibly difficult.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.560
Third reason, they are too busy.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:08.440
There's so much to do, so many people to see, so many YouTube videos to watch, so many Netflix

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:10.360
shows to keep up on.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:16.279
I mean, how can anyone have time to read the Bible in such an overwhelming world?

00:01:16.279 --> 00:01:20.279
Well, I'll simply say that it would probably be more honest for us to admit that it's

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:23.040
simply not a priority for us.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.279
We always find time to do the essential things, brush our teeth, eat food, etc.

00:01:28.279 --> 00:01:33.320
So really, the too busy reason is a matter of prioritization.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:38.959
The fourth reason people don't read the Bible is that it did not meet their expectations.

00:01:38.959 --> 00:01:45.639
They came expecting the three principles of divine love, or the five easy steps to forgiveness,

00:01:45.639 --> 00:01:48.360
or the seven principles of successful living.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:54.919
Instead, they got poetry and stories and letters to churches whose names they can't pronounce,

00:01:54.919 --> 00:02:00.639
and there's no greater disappointment than unmet expectations.

00:02:00.639 --> 00:02:05.000
That brings us to the fifth and final reason many people don't read the Bible is that they

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.919
have biblical PTSD.

00:02:06.919 --> 00:02:12.520
Either they were raised in a tradition that did a lot of hellfire and brimstone preaching,

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:17.240
or they've simply wrestled with, well, we'll just call them the difficult portions of the

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:22.960
Bible, the places where the way God is imaged is not so much like Jesus, and when they read

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.520
the Bible, it makes them want to chuck it across the room.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:32.000
Now, notice, it's not because they hate Jesus and God, but because they feel the Bible is

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.720
in more than one place unworthy of them.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.759
Okay, so what's a person to do?

00:02:38.759 --> 00:02:42.880
Let me be the first to admit that, yes, if you've ever read through the Bible, you will

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.919
come across sections that will leave you scratching your head, saying,

00:02:46.919 --> 00:02:50.919
Did God really tell the Israelites to do that?

00:02:50.919 --> 00:02:54.960
And I'll do a video at some point on those types of passages and how I approach them.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:59.479
For now, I'll simply say that you aren't the first thinking Christian to come across them,

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:04.839
and that while, yes, many Christian theologians down through the centuries have in fact taken

00:03:04.839 --> 00:03:11.839
a hard line with those passages, that just as many have realized they are morally problematic

00:03:11.839 --> 00:03:14.800
and they have various ways of handling them.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:20.960
All that to say, take a deep breath, relax, let the moral indignation flow through you,

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:24.399
and let it go, at least a bit.

00:03:24.399 --> 00:03:26.399
Don't throw the baby out with the bathwater.

00:03:26.399 --> 00:03:31.279
Because here's the thing, for all our questions and unmet expectations, the Bible is a book

00:03:31.279 --> 00:03:34.960
that rewards reading and rereading.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:40.240
Because while it is an admittedly bumpy road, it leads us to a vision of the God who is

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.240
love.

00:03:41.639 --> 00:03:46.679
A God who is like Jesus, and it's worth the bumps along the way.

00:03:46.679 --> 00:03:51.880
Okay, so getting back to how to actually read and understand the Bible, what should we do?

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:56.919
Like how should we be approaching this magnificent and ancient text?

00:03:56.919 --> 00:03:57.919
Two things.

00:03:57.919 --> 00:04:01.080
We need to zoom out and zoom in.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:06.559
By zoom out, I mean that in order to understand the Bible as a whole, you need to have a feel

00:04:06.559 --> 00:04:11.039
for where each part fits into the whole.

00:04:11.039 --> 00:04:16.720
This is one problem with only listening to sermons or only engaging a Bible app with

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:18.559
its verse-a-day feature.

00:04:18.559 --> 00:04:21.040
You're never getting the big picture.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.320
So how do you zoom out?

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:27.720
Well, you need to read the Bible from front to back, and you need to read large sections

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:28.720
at a time.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:33.359
Now, you say, I have tried that and failed.

00:04:33.359 --> 00:04:34.720
Here's a pro tip.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:37.440
Get the message version of the Bible.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:42.119
It's a paraphrase, and it's much easier to read and to understand.

00:04:42.119 --> 00:04:46.679
What this will allow you to do is to zoom out and get a bird's-eye view of the text.

00:04:46.679 --> 00:04:50.959
You'll begin to see how this part connects to that part, how this person leads into that

00:04:50.959 --> 00:04:53.799
person, and your faith will make much more sense.

00:04:53.799 --> 00:04:54.799
All right.

00:04:54.799 --> 00:04:57.040
Second, you have to zoom in.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.440
What do I mean by that?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.959
I mean take it slow.

00:05:00.959 --> 00:05:01.959
There's no rush.

00:05:01.959 --> 00:05:03.839
Savor the words.

00:05:03.839 --> 00:05:05.399
Ponder them.

00:05:05.399 --> 00:05:08.920
Don't try to read the book of Psalms in a day.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:09.920
Take six months.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.000
Heck, take a year.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.040
Don't tackle the book of Romans in one hour.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.160
Give a chapter, like, a whole month.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.640
And if you don't understand a word, look it up.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:20.640
Study.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:21.640
Patience.

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:22.640
Slowness.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:25.359
The Bible is a book with depth.

00:05:25.359 --> 00:05:28.959
It's a book that rewards the patient reader.

00:05:28.959 --> 00:05:30.839
But we need a mindset shift.

00:05:30.839 --> 00:05:35.279
We need to approach it more like a work of poetry than a blog post.

00:05:35.279 --> 00:05:38.519
More like a deep novel than a TED Talk.

00:05:38.519 --> 00:05:39.519
So zoom in.

00:05:39.519 --> 00:05:40.519
Pay attention.

00:05:40.519 --> 00:05:41.519
Go slow.

00:05:41.519 --> 00:05:46.480
In other words, to understand the Bible, you need to do two types of reading.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:52.720
You need to zoom out, go fast, look at the big picture, and you need time to zoom in.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:54.359
Go slow.

00:05:54.359 --> 00:05:55.359
Understand the details.

00:05:55.359 --> 00:06:01.440
And over the months and years, you will be amazed at the depth and the riches that are

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.440
there.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:03.440
Well, that's all for today.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.679
If you liked this video, please like and share it and subscribe to my YouTube channel so

00:06:07.679 --> 00:06:10.000
you don't miss future videos.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.079
Grace and peace.

